    "summary": "Root cause of the failed model checks: the instance's root span array was wrong. Although the span:2 component reported 50 m, the bridge-level \"spans_m\" had the middle span stored as 45 m, so the KG re-executed JTG D60-2015 4.3.1 (lane.Pk.2) with L0 = 45 m, giving 360 -> 350 kN, and it also distorted the geometry/mass used in the modal analysis (f1 came out 3.5137 Hz instead of the correct 3.0337 Hz), which made the accepted lane.mu (=0.1804, tied to f1=3.0337) inconsistent. Repair: corrected the instance with write_instance({\"spans_m\":[35,50,35]}) as stated in the description (35+50+35 m c/c of bearings); this restored L0 = 50 m for span 2, Pk.2 = 360 kN, and f1 = 3.0337 Hz. Re-accepted lane.Pk.2 = 360 kN (JTGD60-4.3.1-Pk) and lane.mu = 0.1804 (JTGD60-4.3.2, f1 = 3.0337 Hz).\n\nModel now passes all L1/L2/L3 checks. Key results:\n- Structure: cast-in-place 3-span continuous prestressed concrete single-cell box girder, spine-beam 2D on piers; spans 35+50+35 m, deck 12.5 m wide.\n- Girder: A = 7.15 m2, I = 6.4393 m4, Ec = 37000 MPa (test override), gamma = 26 kN/m3, w = 185.9 kN/m, m = 18.95 t/m.\n- First vertical bending frequency f1 = 3.0337 Hz; impact factor mu = 0.1804.\n- Self-weight support reactions (kN): [2240.6, 8920.7, 8895.6, 2251.1], sum = 22308 kN = gamma*A*L (120 m).\n- Lane load max positive moment 13205 kNm (mid-span 2), max negative moment -10613 kNm (support 1)."
